<title>USA: TABLE - Sovereign Bancorp Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Sovereign Bancorp Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WYOMISSING, Pa. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ended June 30	   Ended June 30</p>
<p>				     1997	1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income     $ 64,649  $ 60,741 $126,514 $117,578</p>
<p> Provision for Loan Losses  1,000     1,416    9,700    2,216</p>
<p> Other Income		   9,538     9,332   16,905   17,660</p>
<p> Other Expenses		38,496    41,147   74,821   77,939</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes	 34,691    27,510   58,898   55,083</p>
<p> Income Tax Provision	13,185    10,407   20,230   20,794</p>
<p> MRCs (1)			   -0-	 -0-    7,955	-0-</p>
<p> Net Income		    21,506    17,103   30,713   34,289</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share	    0.27	0.23     0.39     0.45</p>
<p>Net Income before MRCs(1)</p>
<p>				   21,506    17,103   41,413   34,289</p>
<p> EPS before MRCs(1)	    0.27	0.23     0.52     0.45</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) MRC = One time merger related costs.  Excludes $7.9 million (pre-tax) of costs classified as provision for loan losses.  Total merger costs were $15.9 million ($10.7 million net of tax).</p>
<p>The company said on July 2, 1997, it acquired Fleet Financial Group Inc's Automobile Finance Division.</p>
<p>The auto division consists of about $2.0 billion of auto loans and could potentially originate $1.0 billion of consumer and business assets annually.</p>
<p>Full name is Sovereign Bancorp Inc.</p>
</text>
